# Aarotech Production Readiness & Growth Audit

This plan outlines the critical steps required to make the Aarotech website production-ready, maximize organic visibility, implement robust tracking, and prepare for scaling. 

The audit covers 11 phases, organized into 4 priority tiers as requested. 

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **User Review Required:** Please review the priority of these items and approve this plan. Once approved, I will begin implementing them sequentially.

## 1. Critical (Must Fix Before Launch)

These items are essential for the website to function correctly, be indexed properly by search engines, and track baseline metrics.

### Technical SEO & Google Readiness (Phases 1 & 2)
- **JSON-LD Schema Implementation:** (Code) Add Organization, Local Business, and Website schema to `layout.tsx`.
- **Google Search Console & GA4 Setup:** 
  - (Code) Integrate GA4 (via Next.js `@next/third-parties/google` or custom script).
  - (Manual/DNS) Verify domain in Google Search Console via TXT record.
- **Dynamic Metadata Enhancements:** (Code) Ensure `robots.ts` and `sitemap.ts` are robust. Add `manifest.webmanifest`, `theme-color`, and a proper `favicon.ico` / apple-touch-icon.

### Production Readiness & Security (Phases 10 & 8)
- **Error Handling:** (Code) Create `not-found.tsx` (404 page), `error.tsx` (500 handling), and `loading.tsx` to handle React Suspense boundaries.
- **Security Headers:** (Code) Implement HTTP security headers (CSP, X-Frame-Options, Strict-Transport-Security) in `next.config.ts`.
- **Link Auditing:** (Code) Ensure all internal links are working and remove any placeholder links (`#`).

### Performance (Core Web Vitals) (Phase 3)
- **Image Optimization:** (Code) Configure `next.config.ts` for remote patterns (if using external images) and ensure all `<img>` tags use `next/image` with proper `alt` tags and `priority` for above-the-fold images (LCP).

## 2. High Priority (Within First Week)

These items significantly impact user experience, conversion rates, and baseline local SEO.

### Conversion Optimization (Phase 6)
- **Friction Point Removal:** (Code) Audit the user journey from Landing -> Scroll -> CTA. Improve button visibility, ensure form submissions have immediate feedback (toast notifications/Thank You states), and verify contrast ratios.
- **Sticky CTAs:** (Code) Ensure mobile has a sticky "Contact" or "WhatsApp" button that doesn't obstruct content.

### Tracking (Phase 7)
- **Event Tracking Plan:** (Code) Implement custom event tracking for:
  - Form submissions
  - WhatsApp button clicks (`tel:` and `wa.me`)
  - Email clicks (`mailto:`)
  - Navigation to Service/Industry pages.

### Local SEO (Phase 4)
- **Tamil Nadu Targeting:** (Code/Content) Organically weave locations (Chennai, Coimbatore, Madurai, etc.) into the `layout.tsx` metadata description and homepage copy where appropriate (e.g., "Serving businesses across Chennai, Coimbatore, and Tamil Nadu").
- **Google Business Profile:** (Manual) Ensure the GMB profile is fully populated with services, matching the website's exact NAP (Name, Address, Phone) details.

## 3. Medium Priority (Within First Month)

These items focus on scaling content, improving accessibility, and deepening tracking insights.

### Content Strategy (Phase 5)
- **Service & Industry Pages:** (Code/Content) Expand current services/industries into dedicated dynamic routes (`/services/[slug]`) with deep content, FAQs, and targeted keywords rather than just anchoring on the homepage.
- **FAQ Schema:** (Code) Add `FAQPage` JSON-LD schema to the FAQ section to win rich snippets in Google Search.
- **Breadcrumbs:** (Code) Implement Breadcrumb navigation and `BreadcrumbList` schema for deeper pages.

### Accessibility (Phase 9)
- **WCAG Audit:** (Code) Ensure full keyboard navigability (focus states), ARIA labels on all interactive elements (especially modal dialogs or mobile menus), and semantic HTML (`<main>`, `<section>`, `<nav>`, `<aside>`).

### Tracking Expansion (Phase 7 & 2)
- **Microsoft Clarity:** (Code) Add the Microsoft Clarity tracking snippet to record user sessions and heatmaps to analyze scrolling and friction points.

## 4. Future Improvements

These items lay the groundwork for paid marketing and long-term organic dominance.

### Digital Marketing Readiness (Phase 11)
- **Dedicated Landing Pages:** (Code) Create reusable Next.js templates for Google Ads / Meta Ads that hide the main navigation and focus entirely on lead capture.
- **Lead Magnets:** (Code/Content) Implement an email capture form for a free resource (e.g., "Digital Marketing Audit Checklist").
- **CRM Integration:** (Code) Connect the contact form directly to a CRM (HubSpot, Zoho) or automation tool (Zapier/Make) instead of just sending an email.

### Advanced Content Strategy (Phase 5 & 4)
- **City-Specific Pages:** (Code) Create dynamic `/locations/[city]` pages for major hubs like Chennai, Coimbatore, and Madurai tailored to local search intent.
- **Blog Architecture:** (Code) Implement a blog section (using a CMS like Sanity or Markdown) to capture long-tail keywords (e.g., "Best SEO practices for hospitals in Chennai").

